# TIL — Day 06: How to Run Ubuntu on Docker for Linux Practice

## Commands to Run Ubuntu

### 1. Quick Test (deletes after exit)

docker run -it --rm ubuntu bash

# -i = interactive (keep input open)
# -t = allocate terminal
# --rm = delete container after exit
# ubuntu = image name
# bash = command to run inside

Result:
root@346d0edf0891:/#
# You are now root inside real Ubuntu

### 2. Keep It (so you can come back to same container)

docker run -it --name my-ubuntu-lab ubuntu bash

# --name my-ubuntu-lab = give it a name to find later
# No --rm, so it stays after exit

Inside:
apt update
apt install -y sudo adduser passwd
adduser mohit
usermod -aG sudo mohit
id mohit
su - mohit

exit
# Back to Windows: Vanilla Test@MW-C81R444 UCRT64 ~

### 3. How to Get Back In After Exit

docker ps -a
# Shows: my-ubuntu-lab   Exited

docker start -ai my-ubuntu-lab
# start = start stopped container
# -a = attach, -i = interactive

You are back inside same container with all files.

### 4. Other Docker Commands

docker ps
# Show running containers only

docker ps -a
# Show all, including stopped

docker stop my-ubuntu-lab
# Stop container

docker rm my-ubuntu-lab
# Delete container permanently

docker run -it --rm ubuntu bash
# Fresh clean Ubuntu every time
